    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Team Paul Reddy are delighted to bring No. 179 Broadmeadows to the Swords property market. Spanning approximately 105 sq. m., this spacious four-bedroom family home features double-glazed windows, gas-fired central heating, a rear extension, a side carport with excellent potential for conversion, and a sunny south-facing rear garden. Ideally positioned within the mature and highly sought-after Broadmeadows development, the property offers a fantastic opportunity for purchasers seeking a generous family home with considerable scope for modernisation and further enhancement. With its well-proportioned accommodation and existing extension, the property provides an excellent foundation for those looking to create a home tailored to their own tastes, needs and requirements.\r\n\r\nThe property enjoys an exceptionally convenient location, just minutes from Swords Main Street, The Pavilions Shopping Centre, a wide selection of schools, shops, cafés, restaurants and local amenities. Excellent transport links are available via the nearby Rathbeale Road, providing easy access to Dublin Airport, the M1 and M50 motorways. The area is also well served by numerous Dublin Bus routes, while a choice of primary and secondary schools are located within easy reach.\r\n\r\nInternally, the accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hallway, guest W.C., a comfortable living room featuring a wood-burning stove, a kitchen/dining area and a spacious extended living area overlooking the rear garden. Upstairs, there are four well-proportioned bedrooms together with a family bathroom.\r\n\r\nExternally, the property benefits from a concrete driveway providing off-street parking, together with a side carport and side entrance leading through to the rear garden. The sunny south-facing rear garden enjoys excellent natural light throughout the day and provides ample space for outdoor entertaining and family use. The property also offers further potential for extension or adaptation, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\r\n\r\nNote: Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate, and photographs are provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "GROUND FLOOR: \r\n\r\nHall\t                              3.77 x 1.24m     \r\nLaminate wood flooring\r\n\r\nLiving Room                     4.54 x 3.35m      \r\nLaminate wood flooring, featuring gas fire fireplace.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining                7.11 x 2.81m      \r\nOpen-plan kitchen/dining. Fully fitted units, tiled splashback, laminate wood flooring.\r\n\r\nLiving (Sun) room 2        4.28 x 2.74m      \r\nLaminate wood \r\n\r\nGuest WC                         2.29 x 1.73m      \r\nWC & WHB\r\n\r\n\r\nFIRST FLOOR: \r\nLanding              2.69 x 2.14m \t  \r\nCarpeted flooring \r\n\r\nBedroom 1        3.86 x 3.36m   \r\nCarpeted flooring, built-in wardrobes\r\n\r\nBedroom 2        3.60 x 2.52m \t  \r\nCarpeted flooring\r\n\r\nBedroom 3        3.15 x 2.70m   \r\nLaminate wood flooring\r\n\r\nBedroom 4        2.59 x 2.42m   \r\nCarpeted flooring\r\n\r\nBathroom          2.42 x 1.79m   \r\nShower with rain shower, WHB, WC, fully tiled."
